# Fiber Error Handling

## Panic Recovery

### ❌ WITHOUT Recovery

```go
app.Get("/panic", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    panic("Something went wrong") // ❌ Crashes entire application!
    return nil
})
```

### ✅ WITH Recovery Middleware

```go
import "github.com/gofiber/fiber/v2/middleware/recover"

app.Use(recover.New(recover.Config{
    EnableStackTrace: true,
    StackTraceHandler: func(c *fiber.Ctx, e interface{}) {
        log.Printf("Panic recovered: %v", e)
    },
}))

app.Get("/panic", func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    panic("Something went wrong") // ✅ Caught by recover middleware
    return nil
})
```

